{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without a store, a tracker keeps its records in memory only. A tracker given a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker(store:)"},{"type":"text","text":") appends each record to it as the tracker’s worker reaches the record, before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"publishing it, and starts its records with the ones the store kept from earlier runs."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore"},{"type":"text","text":" is the store this module ships: a directory of append-only segment files, bounded at 5 MiB unless you pass another "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"byteBound"},{"type":"text","text":". A segment is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deleted once every record in it is delivered."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentStore()"},{"text":" keeps every event type declared with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":" in the program’s modules, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"library’s own; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentStore(events:)"},{"text":" keeps only the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"text":" types it lists. Each record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a CBOR (RFC 8949) map, its event a map of its properties under their names, written through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"text":" conformance. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventMacros"},{"text":", part of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"text":") writes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the conformance, and Swift’s synthesized one works too. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":" writes a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date"},{"text":" property, and each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"date in a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Date]"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Date?]"},{"text":", as the seconds since 2001 it stores, so it reads back exactly. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date"},{"text":" written through the CBOR package’s own form, in a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"text":" type of your own or in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"synthesized conformance, reads back to within a rounding of a microsecond’s scale. Events of other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"types, such as one that conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"text":" by hand without being listed, are delivered in this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"run but never written, and reported once as ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/notPersisted(event:)","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A store doesn’t read the records Traffluent 0.0.44 or earlier wrote, in an earlier format:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" deletes their segments and reports each as a corruption."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each drop is reported on ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports"},{"text":" as a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"},{"text":": the oldest segments","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deleted to stay under the bound, a write that failed, and records recovery couldn’t read or found","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at another ","type":"text"},{"code":"schemaVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A record whose delivery had started when the app ended comes back with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" set. Call ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()"},{"text":", after the tracker’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"app moves to the background, so the records written so far survive power loss too.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An app on Apple platforms that already keeps a GRDB database can keep its records in a table of it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseStore"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GRDBPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"code":["import Traffluent","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\")","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","    var seats: Int = 1","}","","let store = try SegmentStore(directory: directory, byteBound: 1024 * 1024)","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.record